      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Do you have a state that resets the face gesture?\nIf your setup involves using the runtime animator replacement (as in, you have a button for a playable layer that is \"not clicked\"), keep in mind that Write Defaults is off in the states in those layers. This means you may have unintentionally depending on other states to reset this state.\nIn short, have a \"reset\" state on exit from any of the face shapes that sets the blendshapes you use for expressions back to zero. Ensure that either: \"Write Defaults\" is off on all of your states, or replace all of the default/run-time layers with your own that utilize and plan for using Write Defaults.\nIf you need more information on what Write Defaults is and how to plan around using it, check [our docs.](https://docs.vrchat.com/docs/avatars-30#write-defaults-on-states)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
